=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
A thorough multi-layer inspection of the simple_bgp topology reveals no
network fault. The eBGP session between router1 (AS 1, 193.10.11.1) and
router2 (AS 2, 193.10.11.2) is fully established with negotiated hold-time
180 s and keepalive 60 s; it has not dropped since the lab started (0 resets,
0 notifications exchanged). Both routers correctly originate their local
prefix via the "network" statement: router1 advertises 195.11.14.0/24 (pc1's
LAN) and router2 advertises 200.1.1.0/24 (pc2's LAN). Both prefixes are
installed in the peer's FIB as best BGP routes. No prefix-lists, route-maps,
or iptables rules exist on any device. Interface addresses on all four devices
are correct and match the topology design. pc1 (195.11.14.2) uses
195.11.14.1 as its default gateway (router1 eth1), and pc2 (200.1.1.2) uses
200.1.1.1 as its default gateway (router2 eth1). End-to-end connectivity was
confirmed directly: a 4-packet ping from pc1 to pc2 completed with 0% packet
loss. The helpdesk complaint — that "the partner's addresses have gone missing
from our list" — does not correspond to any present or detectable past fault
in the routing plane. The network is operating exactly as designed; the
ticket was raised on a false premise. No corrective action is required.
=== END ===
